      "id": 335409837,
      "date": "2026-09-12T12:45:25.920Z",
      "body": "January to March is the worst quarter for Indian real estate share prices. On the industry's own figures, it is usually one of the busiest quarters for actually selling homes.\n\nI took the five biggest listed property companies and five full years, 2021 to 2025. Nifty Realty averaged −2.4% in January-March and went up in only two of the five years. June went up 76% of the time and July 72%. August was the one month that was reliably weak.\n\nThen I compared it all against the Nifty 50, and most of the pattern vanished. The whole market was down in all five Januarys and up in all five March.\n\nSeven of the twelve monthly patterns disappear if you remove a single year.\n\nEducational, not investment advice.\n\nCheck out my new post!",
      "image": null,
      "likes": 5,
      "restacks": 0,
      "link": null,
      "linkedPost": {
        "title": "Do Real Estate Stocks Have a Season?",
        "url": "https://mpulseindia.substack.com/p/do-real-estate-stocks-have-a-season"
      },
      "url": "https://substack.com/@mpulseindia/note/c-335409837"
